OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774395394
OL,1,Vk4                              G10/24
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGIRAQ DISMISSES DRAFT
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGUN RESOLUTION
OL,4,F
OL,5, Iraq has attacked the United States
OL,6, over its latest plans at the UN for a
OL,7, permanent Gulf ceasefire.
OL,9,FThe official Iraqi news agency said
OL,10,FAmerica wanted to rob Iraq of its
OL,11,Fsovereignty and mortgage its resources.
OL,13,FThe UN resolution says agreement must
OL,14,Fbe reached on the precise border
OL,15,Fbetween Iraq and Kuwait, and on war
OL,16,Freparations from Iraq, before the trade
OL,17,Fembargo is lifted.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FIt also sets a four-month timetable for
OL,20,Fthe Iraqis to destroy all their
OL,21,Fballistic missiles.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG24-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49611
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774395394
OL,1,Vk4                              G11/24
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGSADDAM PREPARES TO
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGATTACK KURDS
OL,5, Iraqi rebels say President Saddam
OL,6, Hussein is preparing to attempt to
OL,7, regain control of northern Iraq.
OL,9,FThe Kurdish rebels said large numbers
OL,10,Fof government troops and equipment were
OL,11,Fbeing moved to the north.
OL,13,FThey reported seeing between 2,000 and
OL,14,F4,000 troops supported by 80 tanks in a
OL,15,Fregion 100 miles north of Baghdad, and
OL,16,F12 missiles which were ready for firing
OL,18,FIraqi refugees arriving in Iran have
OL,19,Freported that thousands of Iraqi
OL,20,Fsoldiers and Republican Guard troops
OL,21,Fare defecting, with their weapons.
OL,22,                           F
OL,23,D]FFromG24-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49612
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774395394
OL,1,Vk4                              G12/24
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGDEATH TOLL RISES AMONG
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGMALI PROTESTORS
OL,5, At least three more people have died in
OL,6, clashes between troops and protesters
OL,7, in the west African state of Mali.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FOpposition leaders have said troops
OL,10,Ffiring on pro-democracy crowds killed
OL,11,Fover 80 people since the protests began
OL,12,Fon Friday. Officials say 34 have died.
OL,14,FAn opposition rally has today called on
OL,15,Fthe government of President Moussa
OL,16,FTraore to resign and demanded an end to
OL,17,Fone party rule.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FA BBC correspondent says criminal
OL,20,Felements have taken to the streets of
OL,21,Fthe capital, Bamako.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG24-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
